## Executive Summary

### Fact
- Two consecutive Intune install attempts for Adobe Acrobat Pro v23.6 failed with MSI return code 1603.
- Post-install detection ran immediately after failure and returned Not detected against the configured registry path.
- Intune scheduled automatic retries every 60 minutes and the first retry failed identically.

### Analysis
- The failure pattern is repeatable and deterministic in the observed window.
- Detection configuration and install outcome together produced a persistent failed state and retry loop.

### Conclusion
- Root cause was confirmed as a two-part deployment design defect:
  1. MSI installation was failing in SYSTEM context (1603) on targeted endpoints.
  2. Detection rule was misaligned to a Reader registry path for a Pro deployment, guaranteeing non-detection when the expected Pro marker was absent.
- Corrective actions were implemented and deployment behavior normalized.

---

## Incident Overview

### Fact
- Application: Adobe Acrobat Pro v23.6.
- Packaging/deployment method: Intune Win32 app package (.intunewin).
- Install command used in all observed attempts: msiexec /i AcrobatPro.msi /quiet.
- Install context: SYSTEM.
- Detection method: Registry check using HKLM\SOFTWARE\Adobe\Acrobat Reader\23.0.
- Retry policy: 60-minute retry interval.

### Analysis
- The process sequence was consistent across attempts: install attempt -> 1603 failure -> detection not found -> failed result -> retry scheduling.

### Conclusion
- The incident was an application deployment failure caused by repeatable installer failure and compounded by detection-rule misalignment.

