## Root Cause Analysis

### Verified root cause
### Conclusion
- Verified root cause was a combined configuration failure:
  1. MSI installation failed repeatedly in SYSTEM context (return code 1603).
  2. Detection rule targeted a Reader registry path for a Pro deployment and therefore returned Not detected.

### Why it occurred
### Fact
- Installer execution produced 1603 in two attempts under unchanged context and command.
- Detection checked HKLM\SOFTWARE\Adobe\Acrobat Reader\23.0 and found no value.

### Analysis
- The deployment package entered a fail-and-retry loop because installation did not complete and configured detection did not assert presence.

### Why it was not detected earlier
### Fact
- Logs show runtime failure and runtime detection mismatch, but no pre-deployment validation evidence is present in the supplied data.

### Conclusion
- Pre-production validation did not prevent this combination from reaching assigned endpoints.

---

## Technical Findings

### MSI installation failure
### Fact
- Install command ran twice and failed both times.

### Return code 1603
### Fact
- Both failures returned 1603.

### Detection Rule failure
### Fact
- Detection checked Reader path and returned value not found / Not detected.

### Retry behaviour
### Fact
- Retry interval was 60 minutes; retry 1 repeated same failure.

### Relationship between components
### Analysis
- 1603 established immediate installer failure.
- Detection then confirmed app state as absent, reinforcing failure status.
- Retry policy reissued the same install command without environmental/configuration change, reproducing the same outcome.

### Conclusion
- Installer failure plus non-detection created persistent failed deployment behavior until corrective change was made.

