## Resolution Implemented

### Exact corrective action
1. Corrected the Win32 app configuration so installation path no longer reproduced the deterministic 1603 condition in SYSTEM deployment context.
2. Corrected detection configuration from Reader-oriented registry target to the validated Acrobat Pro v23.6 detection marker.
3. Re-ran deployment in controlled scope and confirmed state transitions from Failed to Installed.

### Why it solved the issue
### Analysis
- Removing the repeated MSI failure condition allowed installation completion.
- Correct detection criteria allowed Intune to correctly classify successful installs.
- With successful install plus correct detection, retry loop condition no longer existed.

### Conclusion
- The implemented corrections addressed both failure vectors observed in the incident sequence.

