## Preventive Actions

### Control 1: Mandatory pre-release install test in SYSTEM context
- Owner: Endpoint Engineering (Win32 Packaging Lead)
- Timing: Before any production assignment
- Success Criteria: Zero blocking installer errors in test matrix; no repeatable 1603 on baseline images
- Failure Criteria: Any repeatable fatal installer code across two attempts
- Monitoring Method: Controlled pilot report with installer return-code dashboard

### Control 2: Dual-review detection rule validation
- Owner: Intune Application Admin + Peer Reviewer
- Timing: During app creation/change approval
- Success Criteria: Detection rule matches verified registry/file/MSI marker on known-good install
- Failure Criteria: Detection path/value cannot be proven on reference device
- Monitoring Method: Change checklist requiring screenshot or export evidence of detection artifact

### Control 3: Retry-loop alert threshold
- Owner: Endpoint Operations
- Timing: Continuous after assignment starts
- Success Criteria: No recurring fail/retry cycle above threshold in first 4 hours
- Failure Criteria: Same app shows repeated 60-minute retry failures in pilot population
- Monitoring Method: Intune device install status review at 1h and 4h checkpoints

### Control 4: Ring-gated release progression
- Owner: Service Owner (DWP)
- Timing: Every ring transition decision
- Success Criteria: Ring advance only when install and detection pass thresholds are met
- Failure Criteria: Advancement despite unresolved repeated failure signature
- Monitoring Method: Formal go/no-go checklist signed in change record

### Control 5: Standard RCA evidence pack requirement
- Owner: Incident Manager
- Timing: For every deployment incident with repeat failures
- Success Criteria: RCA includes timestamped logs, hypothesis ranking, elimination table, and verified fix proof
- Failure Criteria: RCA conclusions cannot be traced to specific evidence entries
- Monitoring Method: RCA quality review before closure approval

